{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/app at exact clean pushed head d465b450ea3d81a78fe86a7c89d861ad49563f0e on request/config-cross-process-cas, answering 9da2d677 under my promise 91c51d48. Replaces the artifact I retracted at 2df37050.\n\nsave() is deleted. Every configuration mutation goes through Workspace.mutateConfig, which calls the apphost transaction and adopts only the actor map and frontier pointer under configMu. AddActor re-checks its duplicate-name condition against freshly read state; RetireActor treats an absent-on-disk actor as unchanged; rememberVerifiedFrontier judges rollback, descent and depth against the stored frontier, reporting unchanged and storing nothing for a same-head repeat. Rollback guarantees on AddActor and RetireActor are unchanged and no keys are regenerated.\n\nOne consequence is embraced rather than hidden: without the memory-first fast path, a workspace whose stored witness is unreachable now fails closed even when nothing changed. The test that asserted the opposite embodied the contract codex rejected, so it asserts the new one instead of being kept green.\n\nThe cross-process fact at this layer is proven by a real second process that opens the workspace and adds an actor before the stale parent advances its frontier; both the custody row and the key file must survive. That test is sequential rather than overlapped, which is the observed defects actual shape, and its comment says so rather than claiming an overlap it does not have.","body":{"commit":"d465b450ea3d81a78fe86a7c89d861ad49563f0e","path":"internal/app"}}